Content-ID: <Pine.GSO.4.33.0207121236541.28541@raven>


The attached patch (also committed to the sourceforge CVS tree) fixes the
regular expressions in the file contexts configuration to conform to
regex(7) by replacing the use of (|/.*) with (/.*)?.  Although the GNU
regcomp accepted and handled empty branches, they apparently aren't legal,
and are rejected at least on FreeBSD.  Thanks to Chris Vance for catching
this problem.  To apply, save the patch to ~/fcregex.patch, cd selinux &&
patch -p0 < ~/fcregex.patch.  You don't need to run 'make relabel', since
this change has no real effect on the resulting mappings.  This patch also
removes an unnecessary dependency on policy.conf for file contexts.

--
